eady have the raw bytes (e.g. a non-Fetch framework), use\n",[330,1232,1233],{},"constructWebhookEvent(rawBody, signatureHeader, secret)",". To verify only and\nget the raw ",[330,1236,1237],{},"WebhookDelivery"," envelope, use ",[330,1240,1241],{},"constructEvent"," \u002F\n",[330,1244,1245],{},"constructEventFromRequest",", then narrow later with ",[330,1248,1249],{},"toWebhookEvent(delivery)",[297,1251,1252,1255,1256,985,1259,1262,1263,985,1266,1269,1270,1269,1273,1276,1277,1280],{},[330,1253,1254],{},"VatlyWebhookEvent"," includes ",[330,1257,1258],{},"KnownWebhookEvent",[330,1260,1261],{},"known: true",") and\n",[330,1264,1265],{},"UnsupportedWebhookEvent",[330,1267,1268],{},"known: false",", ",[330,1271,1272],{},"eventName: string",[330,1274,1275],{},"object: unknown",").\nThe SDK adds this discriminator to a shallow copy after verification, overwriting\nany wire-supplied flag. It classifies the event name, not the resource schema.\nBoth sides of ",[330,1278,1279],{},"if (event.known)"," narrow normally; no custom type guards are needed.\nUnknown event names can appear before an SDK upgrade. Keep them for triage and\ndecide acknowledgement policy explicitly; a successful HMAC is not a reason to\ndiscard an event you cannot yet process.",[1282,1283,1284],"blockquote",{},[297,1285,1286,1289],{},[729,1287,1288],{},"Always verify against the raw body bytes."," Re-serializing the JSON changes\nthe bytes (whitespace, key order, number formatting) and breaks the HMAC.",[322,1291,328,1293,861],{"id":1292},"the-webhooksetup-event",[330,1294,703],{},[297,1296,1297,1298,1300,1301,1304,1305,1308,1309,1311,1312,1316,1317,1320],{},"When you register a webhook endpoint (or change its URL), Vatly sends a signed\n",[330,1299,703],{}," call to confirm the endpoint is reachable. It's delivered as a\nnormal webhook — same envelope, same signature, same ",[330,1302,1303],{},"Vatly-Event-Id"," header —\nso there's nothing special to parse: verify it and return a ",[330,1306,1307],{},"2xx",". Its ",[330,1310,359],{},"\nis the (secret-free) ",[304,1313,1315],{"href":312,"rel":1314},[308],"webhook endpoint","\nconfig and ",[330,1318,1319],{},"links"," is omitted (it's not a persisted event).",[322,1322,1324],{"id":1323},"signature-scheme","Signature scheme",[753,1326,1331],{"className":1327,"code":1329,"language":1330},[1328],"language-text","Vatly-Signature: t=1700000000,v1=\u003Chex_hmac_sha256>\nVatly-Event-Id:  webhook_event_Qk8pRtSvWm2NjLhYcZaE\n","text",[330,1332,1329],{"__ignoreMap":758},[1334,1335,1336,1343,1353,1363],"ul",{},[1337,1338,1339,1342],"li",{},[330,1340,1341],{},"t"," is unix seconds, captured fresh on each delivery attempt.",[1337,1344,1345,1348,1349,1352],{},[330,1346,1347],{},"v1"," is ",[330,1350,1351],{},"HMAC-SHA256(\"{t}.{rawBody}\", webhookSecret)",", lowercase hex.",[1337,1354,1355,1356,1359,1360,341],{},"The SDK rejects signatures where ",[330,1357,1358],{},"|now − t| > 300"," seconds by default\n(5-minute clock-skew tolerance). Tune it with ",[330,1361,1362],{},"{ toleranceSeconds }",[1337,1364,1365,1366,1369],{},"Future algorithm rotation ships ",[330,1367,1368],{},"v1=…,v2=…"," simultaneously; the SDK verifies\nany version it recognizes and ignores the rest.",[322,1371,1373],{"id":1372},"deduplication-is-your-job","Deduplication is your job",[297,1375,1376,1377,1380,1381,1383],{},"The SDK is stateless — it can't remember which events it has verified. The\nclock-skew check bounds how long a leaked signature is replayable, but does not\nstop replays inside that window. For full replay defense, dedupe on the\nretry-stable, signed ",[330,1378,1379],{},"event.id"," in your own store after verification. The\n",[330,1382,1303],{}," header is not signed and is for correlation only:",[753,1385,1387],{"className":755,"code":1386,"language":757,"meta":758,"style":758},"const event = await constructWebhookEventFromRequest(request, secret);\nconst eventId = event.id;\nif (await store.has(eventId)) return new Response(\"ok\");